-- title:
--   Number of ⟨ T⟩-orbits on SL₂(ℤ)/Γ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number, assumed nonzero (the `NeZero N` instance). Consider the left coset space $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)/\Gamma_0(N)$, where $\Gamma_0(N)$ is the congruence subgroup of matrices with lower-left entry divisible by $N$, and let the cyclic subgroup $\langle T\rangle$ generated by $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, realised as `Subgroup.zpowers ModularGroup.T`, act on this coset space by left translation. The assertion is that the number of orbits of this action, i.e. the cardinality (as a natural number, via `Nat.card`) of the quotient of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)/\Gamma_0(N)$ by the orbit equivalence relation, equals [`ModularCurve.cuspCount N`](def/ModularCurve_GenusNumerics.html#L13), which by definition is the arithmetic sum $\sum_{d\mid N}\varphi(\gcd(d,N/d))$ over the positive divisors $d$ of $N$, $\varphi$ being Euler's totient. In particular the double coset set $\langle T\rangle\backslash\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)/\Gamma_0(N)$ is finite of that cardinality.
--
--   This is the classical count of the cusps of the modular curve $X_0(N)$, $\nu_\infty(N)=\sum_{d\mid N}\varphi(\gcd(d,N/d))$, here expressed on the group-theoretic side as a count of $\langle T\rangle$-orbits on $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)/\Gamma_0(N)$, which is the shape needed when $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ is treated via its amalgam decomposition. It feeds the bounds on parabolic cohomology and on spaces of homomorphisms used for genus and dimension formulas, being cited by [`ModularCurve.finrank_parabolicHoms_gamma0_le_two_mul_genusFormula`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_parabolicHoms_gamma0_le_two_mul_genusFormula), [`HeckeEis.finrank_coeffH1par_le_two_mul_dimFormula`](thm.html#HeckeEis.finrank_coeffH1par_le_two_mul_dimFormula) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.two_mul_natCard_doubleCoset_gammaH_levelH_zpowers_T_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.two_mul_natCard_doubleCoset_gammaH_levelH_zpowers_T_eq).
